# diarie's own .gitignore. It had none — the repo root's covered it, and that file does not travel
# with `git subtree split --prefix=diarie`.
#
# THIS IS LOAD-BEARING FOR THE LINT, not just for git. `check:ast-grep` is a bare `ast-grep scan`
# with no path arguments, so it walks the whole package — and "the whole package" is bounded by
# .gitignore, which ast-grep respects as ripgrep does. Without this file, a standalone scan walks
# node_modules and reports ~25,000 errors from other people's code.
#
# Inside the vp-beads workspace that is invisible: npm hoists dependencies to the repo root, so
# `diarie/node_modules` is nearly empty and the scan came back green. The bug exists only in the
# configuration diarie is actually shipped in — which is why it took building the extracted tree to
# find it, and why proving this package splittable means installing and running it for real.
#
# ⚠️ THE COUPLING CUTS BOTH WAYS, and this is not merely theoretical: adding a broad ignore here
# (`lib/generated/`, `dist/`, a stray `*.config.js`) SILENTLY SHRINKS LINT COVERAGE, with nothing
# going red. A reviewer demonstrated it by appending one line and watching the scan go blind. So
# treat every entry below as a lint-scope decision, not a git decision. (An earlier draft of this
# file claimed the green-and-inert failure mode was "unrepresentable" here. It is not. It is
# relocated — from a path list that a runner can check, to a git file that nobody checks.) This gap
# is now DELIBERATELY UNGUARDED: a `scannedFileCount` floor once asserted it (vp-beads-flr / diarie-agf),
# but it guarded the ast-grep scan alone while `check:md` (remark, also `.gitignore`-bounded) had the
# identical exposure with no floor — an inconsistent per-tool special case, retired. The discipline IS
# the guard now: every line below is a coverage decision. (`brand-dist/` above was added under exactly
# this rationale — generated output, deliberately excluded.)
node_modules/

# Local tool caches.
.impeccable/
.cache/

# impeccable's DESIGN.md discovery symlink → brand/DESIGN.md (the canonical, tracked, linted copy).
# Local-only glue so `/impeccable` resolves the design system. Committing it would double-lint the
# same content from the wrong base dir — remark-validate-links resolves brand/'s relative links from
# the repo root and fails. No coverage lost: brand/DESIGN.md stays the one linted copy. Regenerated
# by `/impeccable init`.
/DESIGN.md

# The brand deploy build output. `brand:build` regenerates it (copy of the deployable source +
# freshly generated stamp + favicons); CI builds it and deploys it to diarie.dev via pages.yml.
# A DELIBERATE lint-scope exclusion per the warning above: it is generated, so linting the copies
# would be noise — but that means a lint rule cannot see it, by design.
brand-dist/

# Local upstream-friction notes against the templates diarie was scaffolded from
# (contribute-back opportunities). Personal working notes — never committed.
UPSTREAM-*.md

# Generated type declarations. THE BUILD THAT JUSTIFIES THIS LINE NOW EXISTS, which is the condition
# an earlier version of this comment set for adding it: `npm run build` (declaration.tsconfig.json)
# emits them, `prepack` runs that build, `files:` packs them, and `exports` points its `types`
# conditions at them. Before that, the package published ZERO type declarations for a fully
# JSDoc-typed codebase — every consumer's `import { computeReady } from 'diarie'` resolved to `any`.
#
# NOT a bare `*.d.ts`, and the negation is the reason: a wildcard would silently untrack a
# HAND-WRITTEN ambient declaration if anyone added one. `*-types.d.ts` is the escape hatch for that —
# the same convention @voxpelli/typed-utils' clean scripts use, and the same one diarie's eslint
# config carves out.
lib/**/*.d.ts
lib/**/*.d.ts.map
!lib/**/*-types.d.ts
